    &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;a href=&quot;{{ url_for(&#x27;index&#x27;) }}&quot;&gt;Back to Dashboard&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
```

- **`templates/login.html`**

```html
&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;Login&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;Login&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;form action=&quot;{{ url_for(&#x27;login&#x27;) }}&quot; method=&quot;POST&quot;&gt;
        &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;username&quot; placeholder=&quot;Username&quot; required&gt;
        &lt;input type=&quot;password&quot; name=&quot;password&quot; placeholder=&quot;Password&quot; required&gt;
        &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Login&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/form&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
```

### Deploying to Heroku

1. **Install Heroku CLI**:

Follow the instructions [here](https://devcenter.heroku.com/articles/heroku-cli) to install Heroku CLI.

2. **Create `Procfile`**:

Create a file named `Procfile` in your project root directory:

```
web: python app.py
```

3. **Create `requirements.txt`**:

Generate a `requirements.txt` file with the required packages:

```bash
pip freeze &gt; requirements.txt
```

4. **Create a Heroku app**:

```bash
heroku login
heroku create your-app-name
```

5. **Initialize Git and commit your changes**:

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m &quot;Initial commit&quot;
```

6. **Deploy to Heroku**:

```bash
heroku git:remote -a your-app-name
git push heroku master
```

7. **Open your app**:

```bash
heroku open
```

### Notes:

- Ensure you have `gunicorn` in your `requirements.txt` for running the app on Heroku.
- Update the `Procfile` to use `gunicorn`:

```
web: gunicorn app:app
```

By following these steps, you&#x27;ll have a basic automotive sales manager tracking tool deployed on Heroku. You can further enhance the application with additional features and a more polished frontend as needed.

